diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-jpeg.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-jpeg.rst
index 9dd4c8d2c7..b55c9b097e 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-jpeg.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-jpeg.rst
@@ -2,13 +2,31 @@
 
 :orphan:
 
-Apple JPEG encoder
-==================
+Apple JPEG encoder and decoder
+==============================
 
 The driver exposes one V4L2 memory-to-memory encoder per JPEG engine. It takes
 full-range single-buffer NV12 (4:2:0) or NV16 (4:2:2) input and produces
 baseline JPEG with the standard Huffman tables. Quality and restart interval are V4L2 controls.
-Decode is not exposed.
+
+Where decode is qualified (T8132), each engine also has a decoder node,
+``apple-jpeg-dec``. It takes baseline 8-bit JPEG with three components in the
+canonical 4:4:4 (1x1), 4:2:2 (2x1) or 4:2:0 (2x2) luma sampling, chroma 1x1, and
+writes full-range NV12 or NV16 in one buffer. The engine writes whole MCU rows,
+so the CAPTURE format is the size rounded up to 16 in both directions and the
+visible picture is the compose rectangle. The engine parses the tables and
+the scan; the driver reads only the frame header, and refuses other JPEG
+kinds (progressive, arithmetic, greyscale, CMYK, other sampling factors) so
+that the client falls back to software. A picture of another size before
+CAPTURE buffers exist raises ``V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE``. Both nodes share
+one job queue. The ``decode`` module parameter (default on) hides the
+decoder node.
+
+The decode sequence is m1n1's (``proxyclient/experiments/jpeg.py``) on the
+wide64 layout: the m1n1 decode block (0x130-0x15c) sits 0x3c higher, at
+0x16c-0x198, like the rest of that register range. The decode MODE value,
+0x777, was qualified on the J604 (both engines; 4:2:0, 4:2:2 and 4:4:4 into
+NV12 and NV16, odd sizes included, 74-80 dB against libjpeg).
 
 The device compatible selects immutable register-layout and identity data:
 
